    <item>
      <title>Covid-19 Delta Variant % Share of Cases Grew Logistically</title>
      <link>https://enriqueacosta.github.io/blog/en/posts/covid-delta-variant-logisitc/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 15 Dec 2021 18:48:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://enriqueacosta.github.io/blog/en/posts/covid-delta-variant-logisitc/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Today, as part of my work,  I stumbled upon the surprising fact that in many countries the % share of Covid-19 cases that were Delta variant grew almost perfectly logistically from 0% to 100% during 2021.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The graph below, which started all of this, should come up if one follows this&#xA;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://ourworldindata.org/explorers/coronavirus-data-explorer?zoomToSelection=true&amp;amp;time=2021-02-08..2021-11-29&amp;amp;facet=none&amp;amp;uniformYAxis=0&amp;amp;pickerSort=asc&amp;amp;pickerMetric=location&amp;amp;Metric=Delta&amp;#43;variant&amp;#43;%28share%29&amp;amp;Interval=Weekly&amp;amp;Relative&amp;#43;to&amp;#43;Population=true&amp;amp;Align&amp;#43;outbreaks=false&amp;amp;country=BEL~BRA~CAN~CHL~HRV~DNK~FRA~DEU~JPN~MEX~NLD~NOR~GBR~USA&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Our World In Data link&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;DeltaShareLogisitc.png&#34; width=&#34;100%&#34;&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Image downloaded from Our World in Data, open access under the Creative Commons BY license.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
